    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Summary\n\n`ao spawn --model <model>` succeeds, but the session records no model at all. The `sessions.model` column is written as the empty string and `GET /api/v1/sessions` omits the field, so nothing can report which model a session resolved to.\n\nThe agent itself launches correctly \u2014 this is a record/read-back defect, not a launch defect.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```bash\nexport AO_DATA_DIR=/tmp/ao-model AO_RUN_FILE=/tmp/ao-model/running.json AO_PORT=3095\nmkdir -p \"$AO_DATA_DIR\"\ncd backend && go run ./cmd/ao daemon\n```\n\nIn a second shell, register any git repo with a resolvable default branch and spawn with an explicit model:\n\n```bash\ncd backend\ngo run ./cmd/ao project add --path /path/to/a/git/repo --id demo --name demo\ngo run ./cmd/ao spawn --project demo --harness claude-code --skip-agent-check \\\n  --mode tui --name m1 --model sonnet\n\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:3095/api/v1/sessions | grep -o '\"model\":\"[^\"]*\"'   # no output\nsqlite3 \"$AO_DATA_DIR/ao.db\" \"SELECT id, quote(model) FROM sessions;\"\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe resolved model is recorded and read back:\n\n```\ndemo-1|'sonnet'\n\"model\":\"sonnet\"\n```\n\n`domain.SessionMetadata.Model` documents exactly this \u2014 *\"the agent model this session resolved to at spawn time, including any per-spawn --model override\"* \u2014 and the schema carries a dedicated `model TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''` column for it.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\ndemo-1|''\n```\n\nand the API response has no `model` key.\n\n### Root cause\n\n`session_manager` builds the spawn metadata with `Model: resolvedModelForMetadata(...)` and hands it to `MarkSpawned`, which merges it into the existing row:\n\n```go\nrec.Metadata = mergeMetadata(rec.Metadata, metadata)\n```\n\n`seedRecord` never sets `Model`, so the base side is empty. `mergeMetadata` (`backend/internal/lifecycle/manager.go`) copies seventeen fields by an explicit allowlist and `Model` is not among them, so the empty base value wins and the resolved model is discarded.\n\nThis is the failure mode the package already documents. `TestMarkSpawnedPersistsChatControllerFacts` carries this comment:\n\n> mergeMetadata is an explicit allowlist, so a field added to SessionMetadata without a line here is silently dropped on every spawn and restore. That happened to the chat resume handle: the provider still held the conversation, but AO forgot its id, so no restart could ever resume it \u2014 and nothing failed loudly, the column was just empty.\n\n`Model` is the same omission one field over.\n\n### Scope\n\nOnly two things read `Metadata.Model` \u2014 the session DTO (`httpd/controllers/sessions.go`) and the `sessions.model` column (`storage/sqlite/store/session_store.go`). No relaunch or resume path consumes it, so no session has been running the wrong model; the value is simply never recorded.\n\n### AO version\n\nBuilt from source at `dbd87a21e` (current `main`).\n\n### Environment\n\nLinux 7.1.8-arch1-3, x86_64, Go 1.25.12, tmux 3.7c.\n\n### Logs / extra context\n\nFound by running the daemon against an isolated data dir and cross-referencing the observed behaviour with the code path. Happy to open a PR \u2014 the fix is one line in the copy-if-non-empty group, plus a regression test.\n",
